    narr:generatedFrom "038ff151773b49d81baa34278a5dac05b09761a2" ;
    narr:narration """This position holds the sequencing debate for multi-site cutovers, and the arc runs from judgment to constraint — but is now itself under review. The mainline opens as [a firm one-site-at-a-time stance with a clean soak gate](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), restated as [a settled decision to sequence singly](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_16) and compressed to [the bare one-at-a-time rule](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_6). The counterweight is [the case for pairing two sites sharing a dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), with two rebuttals: [the desk pain is a solvable rota problem while a double cutover is not](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15) and [a contained pain with a named owner beats an unbounded one](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13). The arithmetic layer lands hard: [a supervisor-count showing a same-week double cutover strips the region's rota](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11), capped by [the flat claim that the people don't exist](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_12) and [the reframing from risk to arithmetic](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), which [the technical rules silently assuming one open cutover window](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25) reinforce. But review acts now contest the settled reading: [an acceptance of the change into this position](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_2) sits beside [a rejection arguing the call settled on two sites in parallel, not a single-site pilot](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_4) and [a change request saying containment did not settle the sequencing](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_3). The register runs antithesis-first with parallelism and metaphor behind it.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12> ;
